-- title:
--   Unramified model for an ordinary completed local ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a discrete valuation domain $A$, a prime $q$, and $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, together with a prime $\ell_g$ satisfying $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$; assume $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ while $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units in $A$. Three equivariance hypotheses are imposed, uniformly in $A$-algebras $T$: that the $\Gamma_1$-condition on a `LevelPData` (the point $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the Weierstrass equation, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}(x_P)=0$, and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) is preserved by variable change, that `IsGamma0PowAt` (a two-torsion kernel polynomial if $p^k=2$, otherwise a cyclic generator-kernel polynomial) is preserved under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`, and that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is preserved likewise. Further data: group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models that are chord-tangent and have the origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal T$ for Drinfeld bases of level $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`, and the two pinning hypotheses supplying graded variable-change and coefficient homomorphisms on $\mathrm{Proj}$ models. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the level moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …` — so $P_0.B_0$ is an $A$-algebra with a point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ representing the functor $T\mapsto$ (elliptic Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, a $\Gamma_0$-generator-kernel polynomial for each prime power dividing $M'$, a linked $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point and a Drinfeld basis of level $q$, modulo variable change) — with $P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A$. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a minimal prime of $P_0.B_0$, suppose the residue field of $A$ is finite, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ with $\varpi^{q-1}=\varepsilon q$ for a unit $\varepsilon$, and let $\zeta\in A$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $xr$ be a raw datum over $P_0.B_0$ whose class is $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$, let $x$ be a maximal ideal of $P_0.B_0/\mathfrak p$ containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $F_0$ be a formal group over $(P_0.B_0/\mathfrak p)/x$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of the reduction of $xr.\mathrm{curve}$ there, with $F_0$ ordinary in the sense that its $q$-th iterated series equals a unit times $X^q$. Then there exist a discrete valuation domain $A_0$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite, equivariance hypotheses, group laws $\mathcal G_0$ and a level transport $\mathcal T_0$ over $A_0$ with the same chord-tangent, origin-identity, section-transport and pinning properties, a fine moduli package $P_u$ over $A_0$ for the corresponding datum with $P_u.B_0$ of finite type, a raw datum $xu$ whose class is $P_u.\mathrm{univ}$, a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_u$ of $P_u.B_0$ containing the image of $q$, and a formal group $F_{0u}$ over $P_u.B_0/\mathfrak m_u$ equal to the fixed formal group law of the reduction of $xu.\mathrm{curve}$ and again ordinary, such that the $x$-adic completion of $P_0.B_0/\mathfrak p$ and the $\mathfrak m_u$-adic completion of $P_u.B_0$ are isomorphic as rings.
--
--   This descends the completed local ring at an ordinary closed point of an irreducible component of the $\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-guarded full-level-$q$ moduli ring to the completion of a universal moduli package over an absolutely unramified discrete valuation base, where the maximal ideal is generated by $q$. It is used in establishing reducedness of the residue-field tensor product of such completions.
